Documented the expanded data model (`#48 <https://github.com/sandialabs/PEAT/issues/48>`_):

- New Baselines page: concepts, baseline kinds, path syntax, rule operators, the ``baseline-*`` commands, Kibana queries and a NERC CIP-010 workflow. The module developer guide has a new "Data conventions" section (protocol names, statistics and live-reading timestamps, the NAMUR NE 107 health mapping, default credentials and secrets, declaring known defaults), and the operate and general API pages cover the new commands, output files and APIs.
- The data model and database schema pages describe the new models, the canonical protocol, relationship type, medium and redundancy vocabularies, the relationships and baseline findings indices, and the ECS 9.5.0 changes. New field reference tables for relationships and baseline findings; the host, event and log field tables were updated.
- The IEC61850SCL module and SCL parser are documented and listed in the supported devices. The SEL page documents the data mapping, CID parsing and known defaults; the Siemens page documents the SNMP data mapping and uptime units; the OpenPLC page documents the new fields. The known-default modules of SEL, Sage, M340 and ControlLogix are in the device module API documentation.
